questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where an in-memory session cache backed by a custom `WeakHashMap` implementation is causing an unexpected `OutOfMemoryError` on the JVM metaspace/tenured heap. The cache was designed to automatically evict sessions when user tokens are no longer strongly referenced elsewhere:

java
public class SessionCache {
    private final Map<Token, SessionData> cache = new WeakHashMap<>();

    public synchronized void putSession(Token token, User user) {
        cache.put(token, new SessionData(user, token));
    }

    public synchronized SessionData getSession(Token token) {
        return cache.get(token);
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where a transactional Spring service fails to commit bulk operations correctly. A custom collection processor updates records in batches within a `@Transactional` boundary, but nested rollback events are being silently ignored, or operations run outside the transaction:

java
@Service
public class InventoryBatchService {

    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRED)
    public void processBatch(List<Item> items) {
        items.forEach(this::updateItemInventory);
    }

    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
    public void updateItemInventory(Item item) {
        // Database modification and validation checks
        if (item.isInvalid()) {
            throw new InventoryException("Invalid item");
        }
    }
}
